B.22 Proof of Theorem 13.1 (MCO Embedding)

Theorem 13.1. The MCO can be embedded into the measurement architecture by mapping MCO entities to nodes in $G_C$ and $G_B$, and MCO relations to typed edges.

Proof. Define the embedding functor $E: \mathcal{MCO} \rightarrow \mathcal{G}$ where $\mathcal{MCO}$ is the category of MCO elements and $\mathcal{G}$ is the category of graph elements.

Objects:

· MCO actors map to nodes in $G_C$ (causal agents) and $G_B$ (accounting entities).
· MCO objects map to nodes in $G_D$ (data dependencies).

Morphisms:

