Appendix E: Glossary of Terms

Term Definition
Accounting identity A relation that holds by definition for any admissible values of the variables
Admissible aggregation An aggregation that satisfies all relevant compatibility, overlap, and identification conditions
Amplification ratio The ratio of total effect to direct effect; not equivalent to a causal relationship
Causal graph A directed graph representing hypothesized or empirically supported causal relationships
Commissioning agent The institution or entity that commissions a cost estimate
Compatibility vector A six-dimensional vector characterizing the alignment of two measurements
Counterfactual design The specification of treated unit, donor pool, outcome, temporal domain, intervention, and identification assumptions
Counterfactual quantity A quantity representing an alternative state of the system under a specified counterfactual design
Data-dependency graph A directed acyclic graph representing mathematical or statistical dependencies between quantities
Derived quantity A quantity obtained through an explicit transformation of other quantities
Estimand The target quantity to be estimated
Evidence chain The traceable path from claim to source to verification
Failure taxonomy The classification of failure modes into nine types
Graded admissibility A multi-dimensional score representing the degree to which admissibility conditions are satisfied
Incidence operator An operator mapping aggregate cost to group-specific costs
Measurement Object A structured object containing value, type, provenance, scope, dependencies, compatibility, overlap, and counterfactual requirements
Measurement-compatibility graph A graph representing the alignment of measurement dimensions between quantities
Minimal core Measurement Object A Measurement Object containing only value, type, provenance, scope, and verification status
Modern Conflict Ontology (MCO) A formal structure of actors, actions, and objects for conventional and unconventional conflict
Observation A directly recorded quantity associated with a defined measurement procedure
Overlap graph A graph representing identified or bounded overlaps between measured cost components
Placebo test A diagnostic test for synthetic control estimates using fake treatment units or times
Pre-registration The specification of hypotheses, methods, and falsification tests before analysis
Provenance The record of the origin, history, and production process of a quantity
PROV-O The W3C Provenance Ontology, a standard for representing provenance information
Synthetic Control Method (SCM) A method for constructing counterfactuals from weighted combinations of control units
Typed measurement ontology The classification of quantities into observation, estimate, derived, and counterfactual types
Verification status The classification of a quantity's provenance chain as UNVERIFIED, VERIFIED_SECONDARY, VERIFIED_PRIMARY, DERIVED_VERIFIED, or REJECTED

