Appendix J: Summary of Fundamental Invariants

The following invariants define the minimum scientific discipline of the architecture:

\boxed{ \text{Observation} \neq \text{Estimate} \neq \text{Derived} \neq \text{Counterfactual} }

\boxed{ \text{Causality} \neq \text{Accounting} }

\boxed{ \text{Overlap} \neq \text{Non-comparability} }

\boxed{ \text{Network share} \neq \text{Amplification} }

\boxed{ \text{Monetary cost} \neq \text{Welfare loss} }

\boxed{ \text{Methodological rule} \neq \text{Empirical hypothesis} }

\boxed{ \text{Precision} \neq \text{Accuracy} }

These invariants are treated as structural safeguards against category errors.

